{title: Precious Lord}
{artist: C. Michael Pilato}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
[D]Son comes up. Blood flows [Bm7]down.
Word made [Asus]flesh; Truth made [G]jest; curse made [D]crown.
Sun goes dark. Love's work [Bm7]done.
Landscapes [Asus]shake; strongholds [G]quake; Love has [D]won.

Verse 2
Precious [G]Lord, please forgive.
[D]Draw me [G]close; help me [D]live [D/F#]for you.
[A]Precious [D]Lord.

Verse 3
Here I stand, no defense.
[Bm7]Stained by [Asus]sin, scrubbing [G]crimson fingerprints.
[D]Son comes up. Day breaks [Bm7]new.
Life beats [Asus]Death; Christ breathes [G]breath; Love breaks [D]through.

Verse 4
Precious [G]Lord, please forgive.
[D]Draw me [G]close; help me [D]live [D/F#]for you.
[A]And one [Bm7]day, [G]let my reward
[D/F#]Be the [A]sight of [G]my Precious [D]Lord.
